# Canary budget page

The document half of the figure-attribution canary. Written to a fixture
tree as `docs/src/concepts/canary_budget.md`, and read only by
`figure_attributions` in `leviculum-std/tests/doc_citations.rs`.

It names exactly one decimal figure, **3.2 ms**, which the Rust half
attributes to it and which must therefore pass.

The figure the Rust half attributes to it *wrongly* is deliberately not
written here in any form -- not in prose, not as an example, not as a
number this sentence says is absent. It is spelled out only in the Rust
fixture and in this directory's README, which the guard does not read.
Writing it here at all, in any sentence, puts it on the page and the canary
goes green while proving nothing. That is not hypothetical: the first
version of this file explained which number was missing by naming it.

The version string 0.8.0 is here so the canary also proves the boundary
rule: a doc comment quoting it must not be read as quoting the figure 0.8.
